  "pull_request": {
    "number": 287,
    "title": "feat: implement storage_key_construction_in_loop lint",
    "body": "Closes #106\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements the `storage_key_construction_in_loop` lint that detects `Symbol::new` calls inside loop bodies where the constructed key is loop-invariant and could be hoisted outside the loop.\n\n## What it does\n- Detects `Symbol::new(&env, ...)` inside syntactic loop bodies\n- Uses the existing `depends_on_loop_state` helper to skip keys that depend on the loop variable\n- Does NOT fire when the key genuinely depends on the iteration variable\n\n## Changes\n- **New lint** in `soroban_cost_lints/src/lib.rs`: `STORAGE_KEY_CONSTRUCTION_IN_LOOP` with pass struct `StorageKeyConstructionInLoop`\n- **UI fixtures** in `soroban_cost_lints/ui/main.rs`: flagged case, loop-variable-dependent non-flagged case, `#[allow]`-suppressed case\n- **Docs** at `docs/lints/storage_key_construction_in_loop.md` with known limitations\n- **Docs table** updated in `docs/lints/README.md`\n\n## Known limitations\n- Only matches `Symbol::new` (future: Bytes, Vec, contracttype structs)\n- Same `depends_on_loop_state` analysis gaps as `unnecessary_host_function_call`:\n  - Bindings/mutations inside nested closures not tracked\n  - Interior mutability (Cell, RefCell) not tracked\n  - Iterator adapters (.for_each, .map) not inspected\n\n## False positives considered\n- Key that depends on loop variable: ruled out by `depends_on_loop_state`\n- Key mutated within loop: ruled out by `mutated_variables` check\n- `symbol_short!`-able literal: double-linting with `symbol_new_for_short_literal` is intentional (orthogonal fixes)\n",
    "author": {
